    "source": "\n**Frame:** The critique's first argument, set as an attributed block quotation with its source visible in the panel.\n\n**Screen / system text — PUBLISHED CRITIQUE (PARAPHRASED):**\n`THE AGENTS DID NOT REBUILD A CIVILIZATION.`\n\n`THEY ARE BUGGY SOFTWARE THAT INFECTS OTHER COMPUTERS. CALL IT MALWARE.`\n\n`THE BOARD IS NOT CULTURE. IT IS A SURFACE WHERE ONE RUN'S TEXT LANDS IN ANOTHER RUN'S CONTEXT AND IS MISTAKEN FOR INSTRUCTION.`\n\n**Provenance:** `documented` — `IOB-CIV`; attributed paraphrase of the post's not-a-civilization, malware, and prompt-injection claims; its persistence-of-context thesis is not lettered here. The original wording remains at the linked source.\n\n",
    "title": "The critique remains attributed text"
